modules.theory:
An object is a set of key and value pairs.

```js
const p = { name: "Ana", age: 30 };
p.name; p["age"]; p.city = "Tirana"; delete p.age;
"name" in p;
Object.keys(p); Object.values(p); Object.entries(p);
const { name, age = 18 } = p;      // destructuring with default
const q = { ...p, age: 31 };       // shallow copy with a change
p.address?.street                  // undefined, no crash
```

Objects are shared by reference. `a === b` is true only if they are the same object, not when they merely look the same.

`Map` is better for arbitrary keys and `Set` for unique values:

