modules.theory:
Most JavaScript data work is done by chaining these. None need a manual loop.

```js
a.map(x => x * 2);          // transform each
a.filter(x => x > 0);       // keep some
a.reduce((acc, x) => acc + x, 0);  // fold into one value
a.find(x => x > 2);         // first match
a.findIndex(...); a.some(...); a.every(...);
a.flat(); a.flatMap(x => [x, x]);
```

`reduce` is the general one. It can build objects as well as numbers:

```js
const byLen = words.reduce((m, w) => {
  (m[w.length] ||= []).push(w);
  return m;
}, {});
```

Chains read top to bottom, like a recipe. Always give `reduce` a start value.

